75:`scripts/cyrus/launch-check.sh [beta|public]` (also `smoke-readonly.sh launch [public]`) is one read-only command that prints PASS/WARN/FAIL per check with the owner action, and GO / NO-GO for a private beta and for a public launch. The collector is `scripts/cyrus/lib/launch-check.mjs` (curl, a read-only psql transaction, `nginx -t`, openssl, file reads; no secret is printed, the Stripe key is only classified live/test); the decisions are PURE in `scripts/cyrus/lib/launch-eval.mjs` (tested by `test/cyrus-launch-check.test.ts`). Each row carries a beta and a public status: public-only requirements (API-key auth, Stripe live, owner-set prices, off-box backup, legal links, eval pass rate) are WARN/INFO for a beta and FAIL for public. Checks: build service auth, promptVersion and scanner hash vs the repo, queue, guard smoke age (`/var/lib/cyrus/guard-smoke.json`, written by `deploy-modbuilder.sh`), launch pair and its pairing with auth, tok_enforce, wallet/storage/tok_live combinations, PLACEHOLDER settings still on their default (list in `scripts/cyrus/lib/placeholder-keys.json`, drift-tested against the settings catalog), platform cost cap, sound-library flag vs `LICENCE-LEDGER.csv`, DNS, TLS (edge and origin, cyrus.my and the admin host), Cloudflare reachability and real-IP config, `nginx -t`, the nginx proxy prefix list vs the app routes (`REQUIRED_APP_PREFIXES`, drift-tested against `lib/cyrus/bridge/routing.ts`), Stripe mode and webhook endpoint, pack store, disks, backup and off-box freshness, alert timer, legal pages and links, sign-up gating, `/api/log` on the Cyrus host, newest eval verdict age and pass rate (`cyrus-eval-gate-1` gate.json under `/root/cyrus-eval/*/`; floors are `THRESHOLDS`, PLACEHOLDER). Exit code 0 = GO for the requested audience. `--json FILE` writes the machine result: `deploy/cyrus/cyrus-launch-check.{service,timer}` (hourly, NOT INSTALLED) writes `/var/lib/cyrus/launch-check.json`, which the admin **Launch check** tab (`app/admin/cyrus/launch`, parser `parseLaunchCheck` in `lib/cyrus/admin/readiness.ts`) shows, so the tab and the command line cannot disagree.
111:`deploy/cyrus/alert-rules.json` now has the kinds `signal` and `cert` next to `http`, `http-json`, `backup-age`, `disk`, `sql`. Evaluation is pure (`scripts/cyrus/lib/alert-eval.mjs`, `test/cyrus-alert-eval.test.ts`); thresholds are Settings with PLACEHOLDER defaults (`cyrus_alert_*`, editable in Audit & settings): queue depth and oldest wait, build failure rate with a minimum sample, `ai_unavailable` + session-limit bursts in 15 min, certificate days left (edge and origin of cyrus.my), error log occurrences per 10 min, token ledger anomalies (balance vs ledger sum, negative balance, reservations older than 2 h), webhook failures (dead letters + Stripe webhook errors). Existing: health down/degraded, backup age, disks (both hosts), AI spend 24 h, storage quota breaches, webhook dead letters.
142:What "accepted" means: a completed eval run (`/root/cyrus-eval/<tag>/`, journal + `baseline.json` + `report.md` written by `scripts/cyrus/eval-run.ts`) that the owner has read and committed as the reference every later gate run is compared with. Without it the gate verdict is `no-reference` (WARN) and `deploy-modbuilder.sh REQUIRE_EVAL_GATE=yes` has nothing to hold an image against.
143:1. **Let the run finish.** `scripts/cyrus/launch-check.sh beta` prints the newest completed run and, separately, a run in progress (`eval-run`, `eval-run-live` rows, read from the journals; no gate.json needed). Do not accept a partial run and do not deploy an image while it runs (the build service must be idle).
144:2. **Read the numbers.** `npx tsx scripts/cyrus/eval-journal-stats.ts /root/cyrus-eval/<tag> --compare /root/cyrus-eval/<previous tag>`: pass@1, final pass, repair share, top repair triggers, failing prompts. Acceptance bar (PLACEHOLDER, owner can change): final pass >= 90%, pass@1 >= 40% (launch check floors `THRESHOLDS.evalMinFinalPassPct`/`evalMinPassAt1Pct`), real boot rate >= 95% of passed builds, no lane with final pass below 80%, no failure class without a named cause.
145:3. **Re-score as a gate run, no spend:** `npx tsx scripts/cyrus/eval-gate.ts --journal /root/cyrus-eval/<tag> --tag accept-<tag>` (writes `gate.json`, schema `cyrus-eval-gate-1`, which the launch check also reads).
146:4. **Accept, in a reviewed branch:** `cp /root/cyrus-eval/<tag>/baseline.json services/modbuilder/eval/baseline.json`, then `npx tsx scripts/cyrus/eval-gate.ts --journal /root/cyrus-eval/<tag> --tag accept-<tag> --accept --accept-recorded` (writes `services/modbuilder/eval/gate-accepted.json`). Commit both files; the commit message names the tag, image and numbers.
147:5. **Verify:** `scripts/cyrus/launch-check.sh beta` shows `eval` and `eval-run` PASS; the weekly timer (`eval-gate-weekly.sh`, needs `CYRUS_EVAL_GATE_BUDGET_USD`) then compares every future image against it.

